                <div purpose="feature-text">
                  <p>There’s no built-in Linux lock or wipe. The laptops your engineers live on end up in a different tool, or in none.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div purpose="feature-item">
                <div purpose="feature-headline">
                  <img alt="Waiting" purpose="feature-icon" src="/images/icon-person-19x24@2x.png">
                  <h5>Your data is already old</h5>
                </div>
                <div purpose="feature-text">
                  <p>Workspace ONE reports on sync intervals. When security asks which laptops are exposed right now, you answer with whatever the last check-in said.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div purpose="feature-item">
                <div purpose="feature-headline">
                  <img alt="Server" purpose="feature-icon" src="/images/icon-ios-24x24@2x.png">
                  <h5>Your own data center isn’t welcome</h5>
