      <div purpose="section" id="migration">
        <div purpose="section-with-image">
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <h3>Migration: what most teams get wrong</h3>
            <p>Most teams never try. They assume leaving Workspace ONE means wiping every device and enrolling everyone again. It doesn’t. Macs, iPhones, and iPads move through Apple’s native MDM migration with no factory reset. Windows and Linux move with Fleet’s migration scripts, so nobody re-enrolls or loses data. Run Fleet next to Workspace ONE, move one group at a time, and people keep working through it.</p>
            <div purpose="section-buttons">
              <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="section-image">
            <img alt="Device health checks passing after migration" src="/images/what-stays-what-goes-800x600@2x.png">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="page-section">
        <div purpose="comparison">
          <div purpose="comparison-intro">
            <h2>Fleet vs. Workspace ONE</h2>
            <p>Workspace ONE has been an enterprise standard for a long time, and it covers a lot of devices. Here is where the two differ.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="comparison-grid">
            <div purpose="comparison-head">
              <span>Capability</span>
              <span>Fleet</span>
              <span>Workspace ONE</span>
            </div>
            <% [
              { capability: 'macOS, Windows, iOS, iPadOS, and Android',
                fleet: { mark: 'yes', text: 'Supported' },
                other: { mark: 'yes', text: 'Supported' } },
              { capability: 'Linux, including remote lock and wipe',
                fleet: { mark: 'yes', text: 'Supported' },
                other: { mark: 'no', text: 'No built-in Linux support' } },
              { capability: 'How fresh device data is',
                fleet: { mark: 'yes', text: 'Under 30 seconds' },
                other: { mark: 'part', text: 'Standard sync intervals' } },
              { capability: 'Vulnerability detection',
                fleet: { mark: 'yes', text: 'Built in, on every OS' },
                other: { mark: 'part', text: 'Windows, through Workspace ONE Intelligence' } },
              { capability: 'File integrity monitoring, policy scoring, and incident response',
                fleet: { mark: 'yes', text: 'Included' },
                other: { mark: 'part', text: 'Through third-party integrations' } },
              { capability: 'Configuration as code (GitOps)',
                fleet: { mark: 'yes', text: 'Built in' },
                other: { mark: 'no', text: 'Not supported natively' } },
              { capability: 'Running on your own infrastructure',
                fleet: { mark: 'yes', text: 'Same features as Fleet-hosted' },
                other: { mark: 'part', text: 'Cloud preferred, on-prem discouraged' } },
              { capability: 'API',
                fleet: { mark: 'yes', text: 'One REST API' },
                other: { mark: 'part', text: 'Multiple APIs' } },
            ].forEach((row)=>{ %>
            <div purpose="comparison-row">
              <div purpose="comparison-capability"><%= row.capability %></div>
              <% [{key: 'fleet', label: 'Fleet'}, {key: 'other', label: 'Workspace ONE'}].forEach((product)=>{ var cell = row[product.key]; %>
              <div purpose="comparison-cell" class="<%= cell.mark %>">
                <span purpose="comparison-label"><%= product.label %></span>
                <span purpose="comparison-value"><%= cell.text %></span>
              </div>
              <% }); %>
            </div>
            <% }); %>
          </div>
          <p purpose="comparison-note"><a href="/compare/workspace-one-vs-fleet#key-differences">See the full comparison</a>.</p>
          <div purpose="callout">
            <div purpose="callout-text">
              <h3>None of this is unusual, and you don’t have to fix it alone</h3>
              <p>Talk to a Fleet engineer about how your move would stage, and which add-on tools you could drop.</p>
            </div>
            <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="features-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Everything you use Workspace ONE for, plus what you buy from its partners</h2>
          <p>One platform for every operating system you run, with the security pieces already in it.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-with-image-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Live answers about any device" src="/images/mdm-visibility-800x450@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Live answers about any device</h5>
              <p>Ask which laptops are missing an update, a profile, or an app. Fleet answers from the device itself in under 30 seconds.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Vulnerabilities found on installed software" src="/images/homepage-vulnerability-management-table-617x440@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Vulnerabilities on every OS</h5>
              <p>Installed software is checked against NVD, CISA’s Known Exploited Vulnerabilities list, and EPSS scores, so you fix what’s most likely to be exploited first.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Filtering devices by platform in Fleet: macOS, Windows, Linux, ChromeOS, iOS, iPadOS, and Android" src="/images/linux-mdm-built-for-linux-600x450@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Linux in the same place as everything else</h5>
              <p>One inventory and one set of policies for Macs, Windows, and Linux, with lock and wipe on all three.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Deploying software from Fleet" src="/images/mdm-software-management-800x600@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Patching that doesn’t wait for you</h5>
              <p>Deploy from a catalog of 1,000+ <a href="/software-catalog">Fleet-maintained apps</a>, the app stores, or your own packages. Fleet installs the update when a device falls out of policy.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="A GitOps workflow for device configuration" src="/images/fleet-gitops-workflow-471x337@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Every change reviewed before it ships</h5>
              <p>Keep profiles, policies, and software in git. Changes go through a pull request, so you know who changed what and can roll it back.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Compliance policies passing across devices" src="/images/feature-image-prove-compliance-800x600@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Compliance without another integration</h5>
              <p>File integrity monitoring, policy scoring, and incident response come with Fleet. Failing devices can fix themselves automatically.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

